abstract: >-
  Clean-room cryptographic refactoring of legacy SecMesh (aff7dc6) rebuilt atop
  Tsotchke's MIT/Apache-2.0 stack (moonlab, QGTL, libirrep, spin_based_neural_network,
  Eshkol, Rosette-Wire, pq-consensus-bandwidth) into a Post-Quantum and
  Post-Super-Intelligence (information-theoretic) defense suite, with two companion
  AMS-LaTeX white papers. It includes 28 zero-Mathlib Lean 4.35.0 theorem statements,
  checked in 6 kernel runs (5 distinct implementations) via lake comparator --paranoid.
  The Lean statements are elementary integer, Boolean and polynomial identities and
  inequalities behind known results (Shamir sharing, Reed-Solomon decoding, ML-KEM
  parameter arithmetic, the Jakob-Bergou complementarity identity, the final
  Cauchy-Schwarz step of Toner-Verstraete CHSH monogamy, classical Fuchs-van de Graaf
  bounds); their quantum, probabilistic and protocol readings are paper-level. The
  Lean Compress_1 model differs from FIPS 203 at x = 832 (see ERRATA.md).
